{"id":"chatcmpl-542a65e5-6928-44a1-bea3-914973ba22df","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229375,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"The task required distinguishing between two laterally-mirrored findings (left vs right lower lobe atelectasis) where the key challenge is correct side attribution on a radiograph. The successful strategy combined an expert visual assessment, a grounded localization tool to verify side via image coordinates, and an explicit verification step to reconcile conflicting signals (negative report vs. positive grounding). The decisive evidence was the grounding box's position on the patient-right (image-left) side, which was audited before committing to the answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When options differ only by laterality (left vs right), prioritize tools that return spatial coordinates or side labels over free-text descriptions, since side attribution is the crux of the decision.\",\n    \"When a report tool returns negative/empty findings but another tool suggests a positive finding, treat the conflict as a signal to run a targeted grounding query rather than defaulting to either source.\",\n    \"Use a phrase-grounding probe on the leading hypothesis to test whether a localized region actually supports it; absence or misplacement of the box weakens that hypothesis and prompts testing the alternative.\",\n    \"Insert an explicit verification/audit step before finalizing when evidence sources disagree, checking that the localized region semantically matches the proposed finding rather than a mislabeled or false-positive match.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging multiple-choice\": \"For lateralized findings, anchor the decision on coordinate-based localization (patient-right = image-left) and cross-check against any free-text report; resolve conflicts with a targeted grounding query.\",\n    \"Conflicting tool outputs\": \"When one tool is negative and another positive, don't average or default—run a discriminating probe (e.g., phrase grounding) that can independently confirm or refute the leading hypothesis.\",\n    \"Hypothesis testing under uncertainty\": \"Form the leading hypothesis, probe it with a tool that yields falsifiable evidence (location, presence), and only commit after the probe's output is consistent with the hypothesis.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the grounding/localization result places the finding on the correct patient side (remember image-left = patient-right) before selecting a laterality option.\",\n    \"Reconcile any negative report against positive localization evidence via an explicit verification note, ensuring the localized region truly corresponds to the proposed finding.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":685,"total_tokens":1168,"completion_tokens":483,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":685},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":483}}}